Add a `CommandHistory` module to the existing `rat-widgets` crate in `/home/brittonr/git/rattoolkit/crates/rat-widgets/`.

This is a bounded, navigable command history buffer with optional JSON persistence. It's being extracted from aspen-tui's SQL query history into a generic, reusable component.

## What to build

A `CommandHistory` struct that provides REPL-style command history navigation:
- Bounded entry count (configurable max, default 100)
- Up/Down navigation through previous entries
- Dedup (skip consecutive duplicates)
- Skip empty entries
- Optional JSON file persistence (load/save)
- Browsing state tracking (editing vs navigating)

## API Design

```rust
pub struct CommandHistory {
    entries: Vec<String>,
    index: usize,
    browsing: bool,
    max_entries: usize,
}
```

Key methods:
- `CommandHistory::new(max_entries: usize) -> Self`
- `CommandHistory::with_entries(entries: Vec<String>, max_entries: usize) -> Self` — for restoring from persistence
- `fn add(&mut self, entry: String)` — add entry, skip empty/consecutive-dupes, evict oldest if over max
- `fn prev(&mut self) -> Option<&str>` — navigate to previous entry (Up key). Returns the entry text. First call starts browsing from the end.
- `fn next(&mut self) -> Option<&str>` — navigate to next entry (Down key). Returns None when past the newest entry (meaning "back to empty input").
- `fn reset_browse(&mut self)` — stop browsing, reset index to end
- `fn is_browsing(&self) -> bool`
- `fn current(&self) -> Option<&str>` — current entry if browsing
- `fn entries(&self) -> &[String]` — all entries (for persistence)
- `fn len(&self) -> usize`
- `fn is_empty(&self) -> bool`
- `fn clear(&mut self)`
- `fn position(&self) -> (usize, usize)` — (current_index + 1, total) for display like "[3/15]"

For persistence, add feature-gated helpers (behind a `persistence` feature that's default-on):
- `fn load_json(path: &std::path::Path, max_entries: usize) -> Self` — load from JSON file, returns empty if file missing/invalid
- `fn save_json(&self, path: &std::path::Path)` — save to JSON file, create parent dirs, silently ignore errors

## Implementation details

The `add` method:
```rust
pub fn add(&mut self, entry: String) {
    if entry.trim().is_empty() {
        return;
    }
    // Skip consecutive duplicate
    if self.entries.last().map(|s| s == &entry).unwrap_or(false) {
        return;
    }
    self.entries.push(entry);
    // Evict oldest if over max
    if self.entries.len() > self.max_entries {
        self.entries.remove(0);
    }
    // Reset navigation
    self.index = self.entries.len();
    self.browsing = false;
}
```

The `prev` method:
```rust
pub fn prev(&mut self) -> Option<&str> {
    if self.entries.is_empty() {
        return None;
    }
    if !self.browsing {
        self.browsing = true;
        self.index = self.entries.len();
    }
    if self.index > 0 {
        self.index -= 1;
        Some(&self.entries[self.index])
    } else {
        Some(&self.entries[0]) // stay at first
    }
}
```

The `next` method:
```rust
pub fn next(&mut self) -> Option<&str> {
    if !self.browsing || self.entries.is_empty() {
        return None;
    }
    if self.index < self.entries.len().saturating_sub(1) {
        self.index += 1;
        Some(&self.entries[self.index])
    } else {
        // Past the end — stop browsing
        self.index = self.entries.len();
        self.browsing = false;
        None
    }
}
```

